<<~ ahu #/charge>>

! The charge — a gift announces itself, the receiver ratchets

''Operator, 2026-09-13'' (quote license): on `nexus publish` — //"agree, but this whole topic needs a research spirit to collide with prior art/golden principles/anti-patterns/security concerns (new capability, needs pono design), and a clear lift into lamplighter caps (not kahu, tho many may hold both cap-sets)."//

''The lean the charge agreed with, stated as the thing this carrier tests to destruction:''

# `--apply` ''signs and announces'' on the crossroads plane, and does nothing else.
# The receiving hearth's `kāhuli grammar` — the fast ratchet — is intended as ''the only door that installs''; no offering reader is live yet.
# `--apply` ''never ratchets''. A gift announces itself; the receiver ratchets.
# ''The lamplighter carries the basket; the kahu decides to plant.''

''What the collision did to the lean.'' It held, and the field supplied a stronger argument for it than the house had: the separation of ANNOUNCE from INSTALL reads as the ''one mitigation that survives a maintainer-key takeover'', which every other control in the stack fails (#/security). The implementation now makes the offering an immutable signed record named by its complete record CID. That CID preserves historical identity; it does not invent a global currentness or freshness verdict. Receiver-local causal antigen consultation remains a separate authority relation (#/security, #/closure).

''And it took one warrant away.'' The clause the house leans on — //the obligation to receive is not the obligation to use// — does not appear in Mauss, who argues the other way; and the hoʻokupu reading the house likes did not resolve to a citable source. ''The lean survives on its own security argument and MUST stop borrowing the anthropology's authority'' (#/the-gift).

''What this carrier does'': it names the caps, prices the attacks, bounds `--apply`, proves the anti-roster stance against the systems that took the other road, and plans the lift red-by-red. It changes no code.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-house-today>>

!! The house today — what the founding hearth already built

!!! The source-local door, read-only, with the offering HELD

`lares nexus publish plugins` reads the operator's own collection and builds nothing. `--apply` remains a loud held refusal in the CLI; the source-local closure must mint the signed record, verify it, write one additive announcement, and report the resulting offering CID. A tier named at the wrong door still draws a refusal that points rather than shrugs.

!!! The immutable record — one offeror, one region, one signature, one record CID

`packages/lararium-mesh/src/plugin-offering.ts` carries the whole ruling in a field set: `kind` · `offeror` (//"an ed25519 verifying-key hex — a nym, never a roster seat"//) · `pluginsCid` · canonical `blobs` · `sig`. `pluginOfferingRecordBytes` hashes the complete signed record into `pluginOfferingCid`; the signature makes two offerors' otherwise identical collections distinct. ''There is no slot for a co-signer.'' The mint takes the signing hand as a parameter and no seed reaches the mesh module.

!!! The verify RECOMPUTES, and that is the load-bearing move

`verifyPluginOffering` checks the signature over the offering's own bytes AND folds the blobs back through `computePluginsCid` — the same function the genesis bake runs. Both halves fail closed. A signed offering whose blobs fold elsewhere refuses; the signature never stands in for the fold. `verifiedPluginOfferingsFromDoc` repeats this certification after a public board has been shape-filtered.

<<~ has Built Record "at/plugin-offering.ts:36-45 carries/kind·offeror·pluginsCid·blobs·sig ~ ONE signature, no steward set (operator ruling, dcec1ef0b)">>
<<~ has Built Verify "at/plugin-offering.ts:76-92 does/signature-over-own-bytes AND blobs-fold-to-declared-region ~ fail-closed in both halves">>
<<~ has Built Antigen "at/offering-antigen.ts does/fold VERIFIED causal quorum acts into held·withdrawn·unsettled·unavailable or no verdict ~ audit records retain rejected candidates, and the fold carries NO presentations">>
<<~ has Built Presentation "at/offering-antigen.ts does/a tender says what it noticed ~ zero threshold weight; five honest presentations move a verdict exactly as far as none">>
<<~ has Built Domains "at/domains.ts:133,142,150 holds/plugin-offering ⊥ offering-presentation ⊥ offering-kapae ~ a signature over one can never verify as another">>

!!! The immune half stands READY, not live

The module header says it plainly: nothing calls this fold, so the law stands READY rather than enforced. The test weld fails when a production caller appears and names the cure. ''An auditor reading the offering path must not take a ready function for a live one.''

!!! ★ THE CAUSAL SPLIT THE HOUSE NOW NAMES ★

The offering record is immutable and content-addressed; there is no scalar currentness field to supersede it. `OfferingKapaeEntry` is a separate semantic act with an `actCid`, canonical `parents`, and a charter fence. Its fixed-point authority fold retains causal closure and returns `held`, `withdrawn`, `unsettled`, `unavailable`, or no verdict. `auditOfferingAntigen` reports rejected candidates as audit evidence without allowing them to manufacture authority. This is historical identity plus receiver-local relation evidence, never a scalar winner.

!!! The announce lane now carries the complete signed record

`offering-announce.ts` defines `PLUGIN_OFFERING_ANNOUNCE_DOMAIN`, `PluginOfferingAnnounce`, and `offeringAnnounceKey`. `writeOfferingAnnounce` keys the public record by the complete `pluginOfferingCid` and carries the signed offering itself, so two offerors announcing the same region remain distinct. `offeringAnnouncesFromDoc` shape-filters raw board records only; `verifyOfferingAnnounce` independently checks the announcement CID, the offeror signature, and the recomputed region. This is additive carriage, not a registry and not an authority verdict.

!!! The fetch door exists too

`packages/lararium-node/src/bulb-read-face.ts:5-8` serves `/bulb/<cid>.bin` and `/cas/<cid>` GET-only, PUBLIC-floor only, //"bytes named by their own hash, no sync session"// (`:18-19`). `:99` holds the line a taker's blobs must never cross: //"a CONTRACT book rides the realm's own lane, never the shore"//.

!!! What stands HELD

